  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $a\\in {a,b}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $b\\in {a,b}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $c$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $d\\in {d,e}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $e\\in {d,e}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $f\\in {f,h}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $g$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $h\\in {f,h}\\,\u2713$\n\nThe elements $c$ and $g$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${c,g}.$",
